# Work record

The board: units of work, the leases that claim them, the strategies they are
attacked with, and the contributors who run them.

## Note
One unit of work. Only the coordinator creates units; a worker takes one through
a lease.

## A WorkUnit has:
    an id, which is Text.
    a problemId, which is Text.
    a statementId, which is Option of Text.
    a parentUnitId, which is Option of Text.
    a kind, which is Text.
    a priority, which is Int.
    a state, which is Text.
    a createdAt, which is Int.

## Note
The one live claim on a unit. Every lease on a unit carries a larger fencing
`token`, and a result posted under a smaller one is refused, so a worker whose
lease expired cannot overwrite the work of the worker that took the unit next.

## A Lease has:
    a unitId, which is Text.
    a holder, which is Text.
    a token, which is Int.
    a grantedAt, which is Int.
    an expiresAt, which is Int.
    a heartbeatAt, which is Int.

## Note
A strategy is versioned data, never code: the playbook a unit kind is attacked
with, the model and the sampling budget. Strategies evolve; the kernel, the
acceptance policy and the budget caps do not.

## A Strategy has:
    an id, which is Text.
    a version, which is Int.
    a parentId, which is Option of Text.
    a unitKind, which is Text.
    a model, which is Text.
    a temperatureBp, which is Int.
    a maxTokens, which is Int.
    a playbook, which is Text.
    a contextRules, which is Text.
    a status, which is Text.
    a createdAt, which is Int.

## Note
Someone running a worker. The OpenRouter key never appears here; only spend is reported.

## A Contributor has:
    an id, which is Text.
    a displayName, which is Text.
    a budgetMicros, which is Int.
    a spentMicros, which is Int.
    a focus, which is Text.
    a joinedAt, which is Int.

## Note
What a unit may ask for, and its life on the board.

## To unitKinds () -> Seq of Text:
    Return ["formalize", "review", "prove", "decompose", "special_case", "counterexample", "repair", "summarize_trail", "link", "improve_strategy", "verify"].

## Note
A unit's states.

## To unitStates () -> Seq of Text:
    Return ["ready", "leased", "done", "failed", "cancelled"].

## Note
Whether a lease still holds at `nowMs` for the fencing token a result was posted under.

## To leaseHolds (l: Lease, token: Int, nowMs: Int) -> Bool:
    Return l's token is equal to token and nowMs is at most l's expiresAt.

## Test: a unit, a lease, a strategy and a contributor round-trip

Let u be a new WorkUnit with id "u1" and problemId "opdp:116" and statementId none and parentUnitId (some "u0") and kind "prove" and priority 6100 and state "ready" and createdAt 9.
Expect that fromJson_WorkUnit(toJson_WorkUnit(u)) is equal to a new Ok with value u.
Let l be a new Lease with unitId "u1" and holder "c1" and token 7 and grantedAt 10 and expiresAt 70 and heartbeatAt 40.
Expect that fromJson_Lease(toJson_Lease(l)) is equal to a new Ok with value l.
Let mutable st be a new Strategy with id "s1" and version 2 and parentId none and unitKind "prove" and model "m" and temperatureBp 2000.
Set st's maxTokens to 4096.
Set st's playbook to "Induct first.".
Set st's contextRules to "".
Set st's status to "active".
Set st's createdAt to 1.
Expect that fromJson_Strategy(toJson_Strategy(st)) is equal to a new Ok with value st.
Let c be a new Contributor with id "c1" and displayName "Ada" and budgetMicros 5000000 and spentMicros 1250 and focus "erdos" and joinedAt 3.
Expect that fromJson_Contributor(toJson_Contributor(c)) is equal to a new Ok with value c.

## Test: the board's vocabularies are the schema's

Expect that length of unitKinds() is equal to 11.
Expect that unitKinds() contains "verify".
Expect that unitStates() is equal to ["ready", "leased", "done", "failed", "cancelled"].

## Test: a stale token or an expired lease does not hold

For all booleans current and early:
    Let l be a new Lease with unitId "u" and holder "h" and token 7 and grantedAt 0 and expiresAt 100 and heartbeatAt 0.
    Let mutable token be 6.
    If current:
        Set token to 7.
    Let mutable instant be 101.
    If early:
        Set instant to 99.
    Expect that leaseHolds(l, token, instant) is equal to (current and early).
